# What the front-end lint does not read (#14).
#
# Everything tracked in this repository that Prettier understands is checked.
# Nothing here excludes a tracked file. A tracked file that cannot be formatted
# belongs in this list with the reason on the line above it, and there is no
# such file today.
#
# The entries below are build and measurement output, which git does not track
# either. They are named so that a generated file cannot start deciding this
# check's verdict after somebody builds or runs the suite in their clone.
#
# THEY CHANGE NO VERDICT TODAY, and that is measured rather than assumed. In a
# tree carrying obj/ and TestResults/, the check reports the same thing with
# this file and without it:
#
#   npx prettier --check .            # exit 0
#   mv .prettierignore /tmp/          # then the same command
#   npx prettier --check .            # exit 0, and no [warn] line
#
# So this file is a statement of intent that the check does not currently need.
# It is kept because the alternative is discovering the need as a red check on
# somebody else's change, and because the issue asks for the rule set to be
# readable rather than implicit.

bin/
obj/
artifacts/

# Where `dotnet test --results-directory` puts the coverage report the floor
# check reads.
TestResults/
